Dragon Burst 0195: off screen, an alertable wait stops between its 1 ms slices

An alertable wait (rex::thread::Wait, SignalAndWait and WaitMultiple with is_alertable) checks for queued user
callbacks (APCs) every kAlertablePollSlice (1 ms). The Burst Limit's render thread (820EA188) waits alertable in the
frame handshake (sub_822A2E50 -> NtSignalAndWaitForSingleObjectEx) and never comes back to the guest while the
game is off screen, so it woke ~930 times a second inside the wait (Cube Xenia: 1.4-1.7% of a core instead of
0.5%). A slice that ran out now calls rex_background_wait (SDK 0189; weak here, for tools that link the core without
the runtime) and the wait checks its object again. In the foreground it is one atomic load.

diff --git a/src/core/threading_posix.cpp b/src/core/threading_posix.cpp
--- a/src/core/threading_posix.cpp
+++ b/src/core/threading_posix.cpp
@@ -62,6 +62,11 @@
 #define REX_HAS_SIGEV_THREAD_ID 0
 #endif
 
+
+extern "C" {
+__attribute__((weak)) extern bool (*rex_background_wait)(void);
+}
+
 namespace rex::thread {
 
 #if REX_PLATFORM_ANDROID
@@ -1259,6 +1264,16 @@
 
 constexpr auto kAlertablePollSlice = std::chrono::milliseconds(1);
 
+// Dragon Burst (0195): an alertable wait looks for queued callbacks (APCs) every 1 ms slice; off screen a slice that
+// ran out waits for the app instead (rex_background_wait, SDK 0189, in the runtime: weak here, for the tools that
+// link this library without it), then the wait checks its object again. ~930 wake-ups a second fewer per waiting
+// guest thread in the background (the frame handshake). Nothing in the foreground: one atomic load.
+void BackgroundSlice() {
+  if (&rex_background_wait != nullptr && rex_background_wait) {
+    rex_background_wait();
+  }
+}
+
 class ScopedAlertableState {
  public:
   explicit ScopedAlertableState(bool alertable) : alertable_(alertable) {
@@ -1372,6 +1387,7 @@
     if (result != WaitResult::kTimeout) {
       return result;
     }
+    BackgroundSlice();
   }
 }
 
@@ -1413,6 +1429,7 @@
     if (result != WaitResult::kTimeout) {
       return result;
     }
+    BackgroundSlice();
   }
 }
 
@@ -1446,6 +1463,7 @@
     if (result.first != WaitResult::kTimeout) {
       return result;
     }
+    BackgroundSlice();
   }
 }
 
